<!--Post: 5304--><!--Time: 1107041229-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5304"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 3:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He&#39;s listed 8 for us...will he have 13?  I&#39;m just wondering if it&#39;s possible he has a specific number in his head?  Does the number &#40;if there is one&#41; correlate to the number of actual victims or something else?  Reason I&#39;m thinking this is his list of chapters was 13...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5304-->
<!--Post: 5319--><!--Time: 1107047513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Should he begin taking credit for other homicides, the number could be endless. I do think that the police have been shortsighted, being too rigid in their adherence to typical serial killer profiles/behaviors. BTK can change MO and Signature: do not be fooled. Murder is murder. Just how many killers can Wichita have, for heaven&#39;s sake?! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5319-->
<!--Post: 5321--><!--Time: 1107048563-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5321"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, great point about profiling. Many of the beliefs, always presented as fact, and forced categories are as wrong as often as right. <i>Mindhunter</i>-type thinking is largely outdated and much of it was never proved in the first place. The BSU boys don&#39;t write books about failed profiles, but if they did the pages from one book could paper several thousand birdcages.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5321-->
<!--Post: 5339--><!--Time: 1107057519-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5339"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 7:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->John Douglas may not like your comments George..we&#39;ll see which profile fits him if he is ever captured...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5339-->
<!--Post: 5345--><!--Time: 1107060286-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5345"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wolf, <i>Mindhunter</i><b>type</b> profiling. Progressive profiler Mr. Kelleher has said the same thing about outdated terminology and beliefs. <BR>Included are &#34;organized&#34; vs. &#34;disorganized,&#34; &#34;serial killers only kill intraracially,&#34; &#34;serial killers can never stop unless they die are end up incarcerated.&#34; It&#39;s an anti-Ressler post, Wolf, and even then it&#39;s  because of Ressler&#39;s infuriating perpetuation of the serious mistake about serial killers being unable to stop on their own. That&#39;s the one I have a problem with because I saw Ressler less than two weeks ago re: Kemper. Ressler&#39;s first words? His very first words, &#34;We know these guys can&#39;t stop on their own.&#34; John Douglas has <b>always</b>said that many serial killers stop on their own. As have Hazelwood and McCreary. Ressler spoke for the defense at Dahmer&#39;s trial, that&#39;s when he lost me. Trying to defend Dahmer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5345-->
<!--Post: 5347--><!--Time: 1107060395-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5347"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 8:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s right, we&#39;ll see, provided BTK is caught.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5347-->
<!--Post: 5372--><!--Time: 1107070352-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5372"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 11:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i thought the B on the clue number 8 looked like a 13.   <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5372-->
<!--Post: 5374--><!--Time: 1107075204-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5374"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Are the drops with crime scene items part of the &#34;treasured memories&#34; in the chapter list BTK already gave out?  Next is Final Curtain Call<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5374-->
<!--Post: 5394--><!--Time: 1107103476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5394"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 8:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK needs the reinforcement he gets from the attention generated by each drop -- the attention is his reason for living, at this point, probably.  I think that being the glutton for attention that he seems to be, the drops will continue indefinitely.  At some point he&#39;s going to run out of momentos, though.  What will he do then?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5394-->
<!--Post: 5395--><!--Time: 1107103724-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5395"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 8:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wichitan:  I tried to take a good look at the writing on the box during AMW last night, and it looked to me like the letters were traced onto the box using a stencil.  The &#34;B&#34; looked like it was made using the type of letter stencils that are used to put lettering on freight packages or even military equipment.  The main vertical &#34;bar&#34; doesn&#39;t quite connect to the curves of the &#34;B&#34; in this lettering. But the letter B on the box looked too squarish and precise to be a &#34;13&#34;.  From a brief glance, that&#39;s what it looked like to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5395-->
